  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 192, 'Smell a clean towel fresh from the line or dryer and take a slow breath with it.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 193, 'Invite a friend over to help you sort one shelf, and offer to return the favor at their place.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 194, 'Count your strokes as you wipe a surface, one to ten and back again, and let the counting quiet your mind.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 195, 'Notice how a freshly made bed feels at night, then decide if that feeling is worth it to you.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 196, 'Shake out the dish rack and rinse the tray underneath where water tends to collect.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 197, 'Sew one button back onto a shirt from the mending basket, and enjoy wearing it again.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 198, 'Leave a basket on the stairs and ask whoever goes up next to carry it.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 199, 'Listen to a comedy podcast while you tidy, and let yourself laugh out loud as you work.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 200, 'Clear one corner of the porch or balcony and set a chair there for resting.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 201, 'Swap the old kitchen sponge for a fresh one, or run the old one through the dishwasher.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 202, 'Drop off a bag from the donate basket the next time your errands take you past a donation spot.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 203, 'Catch yourself if you redo someone else''s chore, and try leaving it as it is just once today.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 204, 'Get a cozy spot ready before you start a chore, so a comfy chair and a blanket are waiting when you finish.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 205, 'Swap a full clean for a ten minute tidy and see whether anyone, including you, notices a difference.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 206, 'Empty the drying rack before adding more to it, so tonight''s dishes have room to breathe.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 207, 'Decide that pillowcases and kitchen towels do not need folding, and simply stack them flat.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 208, 'Share one household tip with someone at home, like where the spare light bulbs are kept.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 209, 'Tuck a little sachet of dried lavender into a room you just tidied, so it smells lovely when you walk in.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 210, 'Remind yourself that a home is for living in, and a little clutter is a sign of life.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 211, 'Keep a small saucer by the stove as a spoon rest, so the counter stays clean while you cook.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 212, 'Fill the washer only as full as it should be, so clothes come out cleaner and nothing needs rewashing.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 213, 'Talk with your partner about which chores feel heavy to each of you, not just which take longest.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 214, 'Choose a song that makes you feel strong, and save it for the hardest chore of the day.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 215, 'Make a short good enough list for your home: the few things that help it feel okay to you.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 216, 'Collect the stray mugs from around the house and bring them to the kitchen in one easy trip.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 217, 'Find a spot for clothes that are worn once but not ready for the wash, like a hook behind the door.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 218, 'Explain why a chore matters to you, not just that it needs doing, when you ask for help.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 219, 'Tidy your bag or backpack in a few minutes, then reward yourself with a short walk.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 220, 'Freshen the toilet seat and handle with a damp cloth and a drop of mild soap, and stop there.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 221, 'Before you leave for work, wash the breakfast dishes, even if it is only a bowl and a spoon.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 222, 'Lay out tomorrow''s outfit from the clean basket tonight, which puts one more thing away.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 223, 'Thank a child for helping before you mention anything they missed.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 224, 'Water your houseplants slowly, one at a time, and notice any new leaves or buds since you last looked.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 225, 'Fill a watering can at night so it sits ready for your plants in the morning.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 226, 'Bring your lunch container home from work and rinse it as soon as you walk in the door.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 227, 'Clean the lint screen after the dryer finishes, a small habit that keeps the dryer working well.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 228, 'Offer a choice when you ask for help: "Would you rather dust or sweep?"'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 229, 'Take three slow breaths and roll your shoulders before a chore, then begin gently.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 230, 'Brush away any cobwebs you can reach from the floor with a broom, and leave high corners alone.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 231, 'Rinse your travel mug as soon as you get home from the commute, before the coffee dries in the bottom.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 232, 'Leave the washer door open after the last load so it can air out and stay fresh.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 233, 'Show a roommate where the cleaning supplies live, so anyone can start a job without asking.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 234, 'Stretch your arms overhead between rooms as you tidy, and let your body enjoy the small break.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 235, 'Let a paper plate do the work on a busy evening, and skip the extra washing.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 236, 'Feel the warmth of the water on a chilly autumn evening as you wash up, and let it be a moment of comfort.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 237, 'Rinse a muddy pair of kids'' pants under the outdoor faucet on a spring afternoon before they go in the hamper.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 238, 'Let your partner know when you would like help and when you would simply like company while you work.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 239, 'Move a small chore to a spot with a view, like sorting the mail at a sunny window.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 240, 'Put your feet up for a few minutes before you begin the evening tidy.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 241, 'Pause after clearing the sink and take one slow breath while you look at the clean space.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 242, 'Sort winter sweaters into a bin as the weather warms, keeping out just a couple for cool evenings.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 243, 'Agree on what done looks like for one shared job, so nobody has to guess.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 244, 'Phone a relative while you water the garden, and tell them what is blooming.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 245, 'Recall who taught you to clean, and notice one kind habit you picked up from them.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 246, 'Remind yourself that dishes in the sink are a sign of meals made and a life being lived.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 247, 'Move the summer clothes to the back of the closet when fall arrives, so warmer things are easy to reach.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 248, 'Ask a young child to be your helper for one task, handing you things, and tell them how useful that was.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 249, 'Look for one thing you like about your home while you tidy, like a favorite photo or the way light falls on the floor.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 250, 'In early spring, pull a few weeds from one small patch of ground, kneeling on something soft.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 251, 'Think of someone you once cooked for or shared tea with while you wash the cups tonight.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 252, 'Spend a moment remembering who taught you to fold laundry, and smile at the habit they passed on.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 253, 'End a family tidy by sitting together for a moment and enjoying the room you cleared.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 254, 'Use a soft cloth that feels nice in your hand when you dust, and enjoy the feel of it as you go.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 255, 'Put a fan in the room where you do your one chore on a hot summer day, and work slowly.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 256, 'Put away the clean dishes from the rack while you wait for the toast to pop.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 257, 'Tape a simple picture of a shirt, pants or socks on each of your child''s drawers so clothes find their way home.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 258, 'Make room for an older relative at home to help in a way that suits them, like sorting the mail.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 259, 'Play a nature sounds track, like rain or birdsong, while you tidy a bedroom on a quiet evening.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 260, 'Hang a cloth in the shower so you can give the walls a quick swipe after rinsing.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 261, 'Prop the dishwasher door open a crack after it finishes so everything dries without towels.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 262, 'Set aside outgrown kids'' clothes in a bag for a friend or cousin with a younger child.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 263, 'Rotate one chore around the household so everyone gets a turn and nobody is stuck with it for good.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 264, 'Step outside for five minutes of fresh air after you finish a chore, whatever the season.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 265, 'Clear the bottom step of the stairs so nobody trips on the way up tonight.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 266, 'Take the recycling out on a bright spring morning and notice the air on your way back in.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 267, 'Air out a jacket on a hanger by an open window instead of washing it again.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 268, 'Find out from a housemate what help would make their chores lighter, then do one of those things.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 269, 'Vacuum the stairs one step at a time, and count them as you go.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 270, 'Toss three pieces of junk mail into the recycling before they settle into a pile.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 271, 'Flatten the cardboard boxes by the back door and slide them into the recycling bin.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 272, 'Wash the throw blankets from the couch on a warm morning so they are fresh for cozy evenings.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 273, 'Choose one evening a week with your household when nobody has chores at all.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 274, 'In winter, open the curtains wide before you tidy, so the room gets every bit of daylight while you work.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 275, 'Give yourself permission to own fewer cleaning products, keeping only the gentle ones you use.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 276, 'Clear the counter beside the stove so cooking tonight feels easier from the very first step.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 277, 'Put a dryer ball or a clean tennis ball in with the towels to help them fluff up.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 278, 'Speak about chores as jobs for our home, rather than favors anyone does for you.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 279, 'Add one small seasonal touch to a room after you tidy it, like a spring flower in a jar or a string of winter lights.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 280, 'Close the door on a messy room for the evening and enjoy the room you are sitting in.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 281, 'Give the spot where things pile up a friendly name, like the landing tray, so it feels like a real home for them.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 282, 'Carry the folded towels straight to the bathroom and put them on the shelf before you sit down.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 283, 'Wait before stepping in when a child is doing a chore slowly, and give them room to finish.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 284, 'Thank yourself out loud when you finish a chore today, even a small one, and mean it.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 285, 'At work, take a moment to clear the cups and crumbs from your desk, then get on with your day.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 286, 'Add a small sticky hook by the sink for the dish brush, so it dries well and stays within reach.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 287, 'Admire a neat stack of folded clothes for a moment before you put it away.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 288, 'Admit to your household one chore you have been putting off, and ask if someone would trade it.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 289, 'Wipe down the patio chairs on a summer evening, then sit out on one and enjoy the breeze.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 290, 'Once you are parked at home, grab the wrappers and cups from the car in a single trip inside.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 291, 'Tie up the trash bag before bed and set it by the door so it goes out with you in the morning.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 292, 'Hang clothes on an indoor drying rack near a sunny window on a cold winter day.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 293, 'Make a short morning plan with your partner over coffee: one job each, then on with the day.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 294, 'Vacuum a rug in neat stripes, and enjoy the lines you leave behind, like a freshly mowed lawn.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 295, 'Brush off the patio chairs on a sunny spring day so they are ready when you want to sit outside.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 296, 'After the last meal of the day, wipe the kitchen table and push the chairs in.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 297, 'Return one item from the clean clothes chair to its drawer or hanger.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 298, 'Bring a friend along for a dull errand, like dropping off donations, and enjoy the company on the way.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 299, 'Smile at the shine on a faucet or kettle after you give it a quick wipe today.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 300, 'Notice which time of day chores feel easiest for you, and save your one job for then.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 301, 'Turn on a small lamp in the kitchen on a dark winter evening to make washing up feel cozier.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 302, 'Use the lightest laundry basket you already own, so carrying a load feels easier on your arms.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 303, 'Say "Thanks, team" after a tidy together, so the chores at home feel like a shared effort.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 304, 'Listen for the satisfying sounds of housework: the click of a closed drawer, the swish of a broom, a door shutting softly.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 305, 'Move your broom and dustpan to just inside the closet door instead of the back.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 306, 'Tuck the dish soap and sponge into a little caddy so the edge of the sink looks tidy.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 307, 'Notice how much lighter the hamper looks after one load is done.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 308, 'Hold a five minute household chat before bed about anything that felt unfair, kept gentle and brief.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 309, 'Tie your hair back and roll up your sleeves before you start, and let getting ready be part of the fun.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 310, 'Pick one room that matters most to you and keep it the tidiest, letting the others be looser.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 311, 'Match the lids to the food containers in one drawer, and recycle any that have lost their partner.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 312, 'Keep a spare set of sheets in each bedroom closet so changing the bed does not wait on the wash.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 313, 'Join forces with a neighbor to sweep the shared entryway or stairs together.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 314, 'Write a done list after you tidy instead of a to do list, and read it back to yourself with a smile.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 315, 'Freshen the TV remote with a slightly damp cloth while you sit and watch.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 316, 'Rinse the sink basin and faucet after the last dish, a quick finish that makes the kitchen feel done.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 317, 'Fold just your own socks and underwear tonight and leave the bigger pieces for later.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 318, 'Suggest that each person at home put away their own things for a few minutes before bed.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 319, 'Tune in to a favorite radio show or a ballgame on the radio while you clean, and let the time pass with it.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 320, 'Shake out a throw blanket outside on a clear winter morning and drape it back over the couch.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 321, 'Ask yourself what one thing would make the kitchen easier to use tomorrow, and do it now if it takes under two minutes.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 322, 'Try folding while standing at a counter instead of bending over the bed, if that is kinder to your back.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 323, 'Invite an older child to teach a younger one a chore they have mastered.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 324, 'Tidy the entryway on a fall afternoon and set out a cozy mat or a small pumpkin to welcome you home.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 325, 'Put a small dish in the bathroom for hair ties and caps that wander, so stray bits have a home.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 326, 'Mix a few drops of dish soap with water in a spray bottle and keep it by the sink for quick wipes.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 327, 'Empty the small hamper in your child''s room into the main basket on laundry mornings.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 328, 'Encourage a teen to own one job from start to finish, like keeping the bathroom stocked with tissues and soap.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 329, 'Record a short voice message for a friend while you wipe the counters, and tell them about your day.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 330, 'When you feel overwhelmed, tidy the spot right in front of you and nothing else.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 331, 'Flip a small magnet on the dishwasher to show clean or dirty, so you never have to open it to check.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 332, 'Say a quiet thank you for the warm clothes in your drawer on a chilly autumn morning.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 333, 'Learn which chore each person at home actually enjoys, and let them have it.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 334, 'Use warm water and a soft cloth on a chilly winter day when you wipe down surfaces, so your hands stay comfortable.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 335, 'Stop dusting a shelf of things you no longer love, and set one item aside for a donation box.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 336, 'Line the baking tray with foil or parchment before roasting, so cleanup takes a quick wipe.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 337, 'Gather all the towels in the house into one load, and enjoy having them all fresh at once.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 338, 'Find out how your partner likes a chore done, and try their way once.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 339, 'Notice how your shoulders feel before a chore and again after, and enjoy any looseness the movement brought.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 340, 'Fix one small thing that has bugged you for ages, like a squeaky drawer, and enjoy the quiet.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 341, 'Smile at the empty sink for a moment before you switch off the kitchen light tonight.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 342, 'Measure detergent with the cap line, since a little less is often enough and leaves fewer suds.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 343, 'Pause before you say "I''ll just do it myself," and try asking once more, gently.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 344, 'Walk through a room you tidied earlier today, and enjoy finding it still calm and neat.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 345, 'On a rainy day, choose an indoor chore you can do sitting down, like sorting a small box of odds and ends.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 346, 'Wash the dishes in whatever order feels easiest, glasses first, then plates, and the pots last of all.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 347, 'What small change would make your laundry spot easier to use, like a shelf or a brighter bulb?'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 348, 'Divide a big job into pieces and let each person at home claim the piece they like.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 349, 'Remind yourself gently as you work that caring for your space is one way of caring for yourself.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 350, 'Walk slowly around your home and simply look, without fixing anything, to see what you like about it.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 351, 'While dinner simmers, wash the mixing bowls and spoons you have already finished with.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 352, 'Slip into freshly made sheets tonight and notice how good the clean cotton feels.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 353, 'Welcome help from a guest who offers, instead of saying no out of habit.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 354, 'Pick a podcast about something you are curious about, and learn something new while you dust the shelves.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 355, 'Set the shoes in your entryway in a neat row, a tiny welcome for when you come back.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 356, 'Gather the clean takeout containers from the cupboard and recycle the ones you never reuse.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 357, 'Tie a stuffed animal inside a pillowcase and wash it on a gentle cycle, so a favorite friend comes out fresh.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 358, 'Tell a child how a chore they did helped the whole household, in one simple sentence.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 359, 'Polish a pair of shoes out on the back step on a pleasant afternoon, enjoying the sun on your shoulders.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 360, 'Before bed, clear the seat of one chair so it can be used again in the morning.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 361, 'Lift out the sink strainer, tip the bits into the trash, and rinse it under the tap.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 362, 'Stack the washcloths in a neat pile on a frosty evening while the kettle heats, and enjoy the easy rhythm.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 363, 'Revisit the list of invisible jobs with your household and see if anything new belongs on it.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 364, 'Hang a wind chime or crack a window near where you work, and let the outside sounds keep you company.'),
  ('making-chores-feel-lighter', 365, 'Remember that a chore left for later is not a failure, just a choice about your energy today.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 1, 'Call your grandma for five minutes this morning just to ask how her day is going.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 2, 'Find out what time of day your dad most enjoys company, then plan a short visit for that hour.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 3, 'Wonder aloud with your aunt about what she wanted to be at age ten, and let her answer take as long as it needs.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 4, 'Check with your uncle what he would like a hand with, and wait for his answer before you offer your own ideas.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 5, 'Learn your grandpa''s favorite card game from him, and play a few hands at the kitchen table.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 6, 'Pick a regular time to call your dad, and put it in your calendar so it becomes something you both expect.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 7, 'Bring two cups of coffee to your dad''s house this morning and drink them with him at the kitchen table.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 8, 'Over dinner with your dad, bring one question: what was his very first job, and how did he land it?'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 9, 'Ask your uncle which chores he enjoys doing himself, so you know which ones to leave alone.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 10, 'Set up a jigsaw puzzle on a card table at your dad''s place and work on one corner together.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 11, 'Mail your aunt a card today with a few lines about something ordinary that made you smile.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 12, 'Offer to drive your aunt to her favorite lake or park, and let her choose where you stop.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 13, 'Find out which teacher your aunt still thinks of fondly, and what that teacher did that stuck with her.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 14, 'Ask an older friend whether they would rather have your help or just your company while they do a task.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 15, 'Plant a pot of spring herbs with your aunt and decide together where it gets the best light.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 16, 'Leave your grandpa a short voicemail that says hello and asks for nothing back.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 17, 'Walk around the block with your grandpa at the pace he sets, letting him pick the route and the turns.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 18, 'Invite your grandpa to tell you how he met your grandma, and listen without filling in the parts you know.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 19, 'Offer your dad a ride to an errand he has mentioned, and let him set the timing.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 20, 'Have your grandpa show you how he ties a fishing knot, then try it yourself while he watches.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 21, 'Snap a photo of something that reminded you of your mom today and text it to her with a one-line note.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 22, 'Suggest a library trip with your mom, then browse the new arrivals shelf side by side and trade picks.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 23, 'Spread a box of old photos across the kitchen table with your mom and write names on the back in soft pencil.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 24, 'Offer to wait in the car with a book while your aunt runs her errand at her own pace.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 25, 'Teach your mom one feature on her phone that you use every day, slowly and only if she wants to learn it.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 26, 'Print a favorite recent photo at a drugstore kiosk and mail it to an older friend who likes holding pictures.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 27, 'Visit a farmers market with an older friend and each choose one thing for the other to try.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 28, 'Play the song an older friend says takes them straight back to being seventeen, and ask where they first heard it.'),
  ('staying-close-to-the-older-people-you-love', 29, 'Clear the snow from your grandpa''s car windows on a winter morning, if he would like that.'),
